Ah, should have looked at your closest implementation.<br><br>3-4 cycles average is typical, but some nasty edge cases can have an oscillation (especially with single precision floats) which is why the time out. I see nothing special in your code that would stop this.<br><br>Edit: To be clearer, VERY occasionally it may actually do the 1000 loops. And it may show as a bizarre spike in performance. At least doing something similar did for me. Took me ages to find too.  <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_redface.gif" width="15" height="15" alt=":oops:" title="Embarassed"><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=60">dog</a> — Sat Sep 30, 2006 7:01 am</p><hr />
